# `SEQUENCE-GENRE-VOCABULARY`: the `message` model golden. All THREE operators, the
# trailing quoted label, the `[tail]`/`[head]` positions the shared connector
# scanner gives it, `in=` membership, and the presentation keys — everything
# that reaches the `messages` collection.
#
# What the golden is really pinning is that a message is NOT an edge. `edges`
# stays empty; the message lands in its own collection with its source `line`,
# because a message has a place in the figure's total order and an edge has
# no position at all (`SEQUENCE-ORDER-MODEL`).
figdown 0.4 sequence
title "Message forms"
class secure "Carried over TLS"
lifeline c "Client"
lifeline s "Server"
message c -> s "plain forward"
message c <- s "plain reverse"
message c <-> s "sustained two-way exchange, individual messages not enumerated"
message c [from] -> [to] s "labels at both ends"
message c -[inline mid label]-> s
message c -> s "everything at once" class=secure stroke=#1d4ed8 style=dashed note="drawn aside" description="never drawn, authored documentation"
